        "original_id": "7e8d7a21-9801-5e7a-a55c-9ae195da83b1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Fantastic Mr. Fox, Khan Kluay, Rushmore, The Darjeeling Limited, Moonrise Kingdom, The Grand Budapest Hotel\n- People: Roald Dahl, Jason Schwartzman, Wes Anderson, King Naresuan\n- Topics: stop-motion animation, 3D computer animation, comedy films, family films, Ayutthaya-era Siam\n\nFacts:\n- In 1998, Jason Schwartzman collaborated with Wes Anderson on the film Rushmore.\n- In 2006, Khan Kluay was released as a Thai 3D computer-animated action adventure comedy family feature film set during Ayutthaya-era Siam.\n- Khan Kluay is about a Thai elephant who becomes the war elephant for King Naresuan after wandering away from his mother.\n- In 2007, Jason Schwartzman collaborated with Wes Anderson on The Darjeeling Limited.\n- In 2009, Fantastic Mr. Fox was released as an American stop-motion animated comedy film based on Roald Dahl's children's novel of the same name.\n- In 2009, Jason Schwartzman collaborated with Wes Anderson on Fantastic Mr. Fox.\n- In 2012, Jason Schwartzman collaborated with Wes Anderson on Moonrise Kingdom.\n- In 2014, Jason Schwartzman collaborated with Wes Anderson on The Grand Budapest Hotel.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
